Omission
- [N1] Omitted trace (input 2): i1:For TS recruitment -> i2:the first step is to advise unsuccessful candidates. -> i4:However, if the terms and conditions of the offer for a candidate need to be sorted out -> i5:it is necessary to check if the candidate has accepted a voluntary redundancy. -> i8:if the candidate has accepted, further investigation is required. -> i9:The recruitment manager sends an Appointment Approval form -> i10:which is then received by the next level manager. -> i37:If the manager is an external resource... However, if the approver is an existing employee of the client -> i11:they may not authorize the form.
- [N2] Omitted trace (input 3): i1:For TS recruitment -> i2:the first step is to advise unsuccessful candidates. -> i4:However, if the terms and conditions of the offer for a candidate need to be sorted out -> i5:it is necessary to check if the candidate has accepted a voluntary redundancy. -> i6:If the candidate has not accepted, the process continues. -> i9:The recruitment manager sends an Appointment Approval form -> i10:which is then received by the next level manager. -> i37:If the manager is an external resource... However, if the approver is an existing employee of the client -> i12:If the form is approved -> i13:the recruitment manager sends the form and other documentation -> i14:which is received by the client HR. -> i15:The HR department scans the completed form and records the position against the stored position in GovSource. -> i16:If there are any variations -> i17:a complete business case is required. -> i19:The Appointment Approval is carried forward. -> i20:If the position requires a medical assessment -> i21:it is applicable for a 12% rate. -> i23:it can take up to 21 days to arrange and complete. -> i24:The TS HR coordinator informs the recruitment manager -> i25:who then liaises with the HR representative to confirm the offer to the candidate. -> i38:If the assessment is not satisfactory... However, if the assessment is fine -> i26:the next candidate on the shortlist should be contacted.
